# Target C-II — strengthen the `t<=1.860` dominant O--O family to retained pair weight

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only strengthening of `target_c_dominant_double_outer_trains_g0076_t1860_2026-09-15.md`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The `g=0.0076` wide-window bootstrap proves, for every full-core Type-II survivor with

\[
t={q-k\over D}\le1.860,
\]

that the retained dominant outer-terminal mass satisfies

\[
z>2.0783-o(1)
\]

and, after feeding its energy back into the network envelope,

\[
U<2.004193+o(1).
\]

The parent note converted `z-U` only into a lower bound on the **number** of dominant-window complete trains with two selected outer terminals.  The retained endpoint weights give a stronger conclusion.

Freeze the dominant orbit windows.  For each dominant complete stopped train `tau`, let

\[
a_\tau,b_\tau\in[0,1]
\]

be the retained weights of its two outer terminal occurrences, assigning zero to a missing outer terminal.  Then

\[
a_\tau+b_\tau
\le1+\min(a_\tau,b_\tau).
\tag{PW.1}

Define the normalized retained dominant O--O pair weight

\[
P_{OO}^{dom}
:={1\over D}\sum_{\tau\,dom}\min(a_\tau,b_\tau).
\tag{PW.2}

If `M_dom D` is the dominant-window complete-train count, summing (PW.1) gives

\[
\boxed{z\le M_{dom}+P_{OO}^{dom}+o(1).}
\tag{PW.3}

After the source limit and then shrinking the phase windows,

\[
M_{dom}\le A\le {T-q/2\over D}\le U.
\tag{PW.4}

Therefore the exact certificate from the parent theorem yields

\[
P_{OO}^{dom}
\ge z-U-o(1)
>2.0783-2.004193-o(1).
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{
P_{OO}^{dom}>0.0740-o(1)
\qquad(t\le1.860).}
\tag{PW.5}

This strictly strengthens the parent count statement: retained pair weight is automatically bounded above by the number of O--O trains, while (PW.5) also preserves both endpoint measures used by the round-hull cyclic-order and diameter-bracing arguments.

Combined with the current scalar floor, every survivor in

\[
1.84332\lesssim t\le1.860
\]

has a linear weighted family of same-orbit O--O trains with both endpoint measures retained on the outer walk.

The next useful step is to distribute this pair weight among the three exact phase classes and couple its cyclic endpoint order to the near-saturated dominant-orbit crossing graph and Section-157 two-sided diameter bracing.

C-II remains open.
